# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for RustOwl.
#
# Referenced by scripts/security.sh (run_thread_sanitizer_tests) via
# TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=.tsan-suppressions.
#
# Each entry must state WHY the pattern is suppressed, and what would make it
# safe to remove. Silently listing a frame defeats the purpose of running a race
# detector at all.

# tokio's I/O reactor registers a source on one thread and then reads its
# ScheduledIo from a reactor worker thread. The handoff goes through tokio's
# internal locking, which ThreadSanitizer cannot see, so it reports the
# allocation-time write in `RegistrationSet::allocate` against the later
# `ScheduledIo::set_readiness` atomic load. No RustOwl code is involved in the
# racing accesses themselves.
#
# Remove once tokio either annotates this handoff for TSAN or ships its own
# suppression list.
race:tokio::runtime::io::scheduled_io
race:tokio::runtime::io::registration_set
race:tokio::runtime::io::registration